<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ōsumi Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ōsumi Province was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>, covering the eastern part of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kagoshima-prefecture">Kagoshima Prefecture</a>. It was created in 713 to strengthen control over the Hayato. From the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-clan">Shimazu clan</a>, who ruled it with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-domain">Satsuma</a> until 1871, when it became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kagoshima">Kagoshima</a> Prefecture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osumi-province.jpg" alt="Ōsumi Province" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lincun · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%9C%B0%E5%9B%B3_%E4%BB%A4%E5%88%B6%E5%9B%BD_%E5%A4%A7%E9%9A%85%E5%9B%BD.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
